nodes.body:
`GLOSSARY.md` now makes an item managed when Linewright has worked it, and the board shows managed items in six columns (`docs/specs/design_system.md`, The board). Consider an open item that Linewright has worked, such as one it labeled or opened, but that has:

- no status label;
- no claim;
- no run in flight;
- no open pull request.

No column holds it: Triage, Needs a person and Ready need a status label, Working needs a claim or a run, In review needs an open pull request, and Done needs it closed.

The design keeps it off the board, and its item page says "Left alone", then "labeled none of …", the status labels, as today. Another reading would put it in Needs a person, since only a person can move it on.

Spec change needed: say which column holds a managed item that fits none, or that such an item is left alone and why.

Found while working on #784.
